              <h3>Complex enterprise products rarely have a single problem.</h3>
              <p>
                The hard part is usually the coordination: multiple stakeholders, systems, data sources, business rules, exceptions, regulatory requirements and operational hand-offs have to behave as one product experience.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="dark-rule"></div>
              <span class="mini-label" style="display:block;margin-top:12px;">Problem framing before solution design</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="challenge-cards">
            {challengeItems.map(([number, title, text, type]) => (
              <article class="challenge-card">
                <div>
                  <div class="challenge-card-top">
                    <span class="number">{number}</span>
                    <span class="mini-label">{type}</span>
                  </div>
                  <h3>{title}</h3>
                  <p>{text}</p>
                </div>
                <div class="response">PM response: frame → design → deliver → measure</div>
              </article>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ==================================================================
         04 / STRATEGY
         ================================================================== -->
    <section class="slide white" id="strategy">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">Product Strategy</span>
          <h2>From problem framing to measurable product delivery.</h2>
          <p>A practical product flow that keeps customer need, business value, feasibility, AI opportunity, automation potential and measurable outcomes connected.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="strategy-flow">
          {strategySteps.map(([number, title, text]) => (
            <article class="strategy-step">
              <span class="number">{number}</span>
              <strong>{title}</strong>
              <p>{text}</p>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>

        <div class="strategy-bottom">
          <div class="strategy-principle">
            <strong>Product decision model</strong>
            <span>Customer problem + business value + technical feasibility + risk + measurable outcome.</span>
          </div>

          <div class="priority-panel">
            <span class="mini-label">Prioritization lens</span>
            <div class="priority-grid">
              {prioritization.map(([title, text]) => (
                <div class="priority-item">
                  <i></i>
                  <div><strong>{title}</strong><span>{text}</span></div>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ==================================================================
         05 / PM SCOPE
         ================================================================== -->
    <section class="slide soft" id="scope">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">PM Scope</span>
          <h2>Product management across strategy, systems and execution.</h2>
          <p>Hands-on ownership from discovery and requirements through architecture, AI / GenAI, workflow automation, delivery, adoption and operational readiness.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="scope-grid">
          {pmScope.map(([number, title, text, tags]) => (
            <article class:list={['scope-card', title === 'AI / GenAI' ? 'ai-scope' : '', title === 'Automate' ? 'auto-scope' : '']}>
              <span class="number">{number}</span>
              <strong>{title}</strong>
              <p>{text}</p>
              <div class="scope-tags">
                {tags.map((tag) => <span class="scope-tag">{tag}</span>)}
              </div>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>

        <div class="scope-footer">
          <strong>Typical product artifacts</strong>
          <span>BRD · FRD · FSD · PRD · user stories · acceptance criteria · DFD · ER models · API specifications · prototypes · UAT · VAPT · migration · deployment · training</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ==================================================================
         06 / PRODUCT METRICS
         ================================================================== -->
    <section class="slide white" id="metrics">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="metrics-layout">
          <div class="metrics-story">
            <div>
              <span class="eyebrow">Product Metrics</span>
              <h3>Measure the product, not just the release.</h3>
              <p>
                I use product metrics to connect activity to adoption, efficiency, quality, control and business impact. Where a numeric result exists, it is presented as an outcome; otherwise the portfolio shows the measurement framework.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <div class="metric-equation">
                <strong>North-star thinking</strong>
                <span>Outcome → leading indicators → workflow behavior → user action → business result.</span>
              </div>
              <div class="metric-equation">
                <strong>AI / automation guardrail</strong>
                <span>Automation is not the objective by itself; quality, exception rate and human hand-offs remain part of the measurement.</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <div class="metrics-grid">
              {metricGroups.map((group) => (
                <article class="metric-group">
                  <h3>{group.title}</h3>
                  <p>{group.question}</p>
                  <div class="metric-list">
                    {group.metrics.map((metric) => <div><i></i>{metric}</div>)}
                  </div>
                </article>
              ))}
            </div>

            <div class="formula-bar">
              {metricFormulas.map(([title, formula]) => (
                <div class="formula"><strong>{title}</strong><span>{formula}</span></div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ==================================================================
         07 / PORTFOLIO
         ================================================================== -->
    <section class="slide white" id="portfolio">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="portfolio-intro">
          <div class="section-head">
            <span class="eyebrow">Selected Product Portfolio</span>
            <h2>Selected product work across platforms, automation and analytics.</h2>
            <p>Five representative case studies; deeper project detail is intentionally kept inside the individual project pages.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="portfolio-note">
            <strong>Portfolio lens</strong>
            <span>Problem → ownership → product decision → delivery → outcome. Competencies are shown through the work, not as a keyword list.</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="portfolio-grid">
          {products.map((product) => (
            <article class:list={['portfolio-card', product.tint]}>
              <div class="portfolio-meta">
                <span class="portfolio-number">{product.number}</span>
                <span class="portfolio-company">{product.company}</span>
              </div>

              <h3>{product.title}</h3>

              <div class="portfolio-block">
                <label>Problem</label>
                <p>{product.problem}</p>
              </div>

              <div class="portfolio-block">
                <label>My ownership</label>
                <p>{product.ownership}</p>
              </div>

              <div class="portfolio-outcome">
                <label>Outcome / product result</label>
                <p>{product.outcome}</p>
              </div>

              <div class="portfolio-tags">
                {product.tags.map((tag) => <span class="portfolio-tag">{tag}</span>)}
              </div>

              <a class="case-link" href={product.url}>View case study →</a>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ==================================================================
         08 / TECH & DATA
         ================================================================== -->
    <section class="slide soft" id="tech">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="tech-layout">
          <div>
            <div class="section-head">
              <span class="eyebrow">Tech & Data</span>
              <h2>Where product meets technology, AI and data.</h2>
              <p>Technical product management grounded in enterprise architecture, APIs, workflows, analytics, integrations and delivery collaboration.</p>
